+  "title": "GOV-0114: WP-2026-0121 — give the unwatched guards something that would notice (#250 three check_g07_binding controls with no refusal test + #234 the vacuous terminal-demand learning test)",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — remediation WP clustering **#250 + #234** as `WP-2026-0121` / `BADF-DEM-0114`. Granted by SARCHI; queued third under BARCHI-1's serialized landing order.\n\n## One defect in two costumes\n\nBoth are **a guard that is correct and unwatched** — the inverse of the guards this repo has spent the week on. Neither is broken; neither would notice if it broke.\n\n- **#250** (BADF-REV) — three `check_g07_binding` controls survive mutation. They fire at runtime and always would; what is missing is any test that would notice if they stopped, so a future edit removes them with the suite green.\n- **#234** (BADF-QA) — `test_every_terminal_demand_carries_a_valid_learning` puts every assertion behind a `status in TERMINAL` filter, so a ledger with **zero** terminal demands passes having examined nothing. *\"No terminal demands\"* is indistinguishable from *\"all terminal demands are correct.\"*\n\nOne WP because the remedy is identical — **give the guard something that would notice** — and because two PRs would each re-sign `badf/lockfile.json` and conflict by construction. Deviation from one-issue-one-task flagged, per BADF-QA's batching rule.\n\n## Work already measured\n\n**#234 — fixed and red-verified with QA's exact probe.** Flipped all 9 terminal demands to `AUTHORIZED` (zero terminal records), observed **red** where it was previously green, restored byte-identical.\n\nThe floor is `>= 1` and **deliberately not pinned to today's count**. QA's criterion asks for a floor justified against the ledger rather than guessed — and every specific number is a guess about a moving population: **4** when the issue was filed, **9** now (post-#224), **~88** the moment #220 lands. A pin would then fail for being *right* about an improvement. `>= 1` is the exact property that was missing — that the filter matched something — and the only floor that stays true across #220.\n\n**#250 — three refusal tests written, all passing.** Each asserts the specific message fragment, not merely a non-zero exit.\n\n**REV's diagnosis of why `:1691` survived, confirmed:** the existing C4 test drives `self-dossier`, which is the **assembly-side** check (`badf_gate.py:3616`). The binding-side check (`:1688`) is a *second code path enforcing one rule*, and only the first had a test.\n\n**One thing the message-fragment assertion caught that an exit-code assertion would have missed:** my first C4 probe was being refused by `check_schema` — `binding.obligations[0] missing green, seam` — before the control under test was ever reached. A test asserting only `returncode != 0` would have passed while proving nothing about C4. The obligation shape was then read from `schemas/unit-test.schema.json` rather than copied from a sibling.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A refusal test per #250 site, asserting the message fragment — `changed_paths` equality (both a wrong path *and* a superset), `content_tree` vs the composition record's `expected_content_tree`, and binding-side C4 (no red / empty-reason exception refused; explicit reason and observed-red accepted).\n2. Each new test observed **red against the neutered control** before being trusted.\n3. The mutation battery re-run over `check_g07_binding` across **both** owning modules reports **0 survivors**.\n4. #234's floor makes an empty terminal set a **failure**, red-verified by flipping the ledger.\n\n## Not claimed\n\nThat `check_g07_binding` is now fully covered. The battery covers the three sites REV named; other raises in that function were killed already, and no claim is made about controls outside it. REV's own method note applies — their first run reported **7** survivors, four of which were an artifact of pairing the function with the wrong module set. The instrument matters as much as the result, so the battery script ships in the PR body rather than as a described procedure.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (tests only). **Lean mode:** advisory. Shared-surface → QA + REV.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
